// @no-instantiate
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: a DECLARED struct captures an anonymous object literal the checker
// never widened. Three lines, no union, no map, no generic, no lambda, no annotation on
// anything — and the `type Circle` declaration is not used, not annotated onto the binding
// and not mentioned by it. Deleting that one line makes the program print 7.
//
// `vl check` exits 0 with NO DIAGNOSTICS AT ALL and is the ONLY command that misses it;
// `vl check --codegen` exits 1, `vl check --codegen --no-validate` exits 0, `vl build`
// writes the `.wasm` and exits 1, `vl run` exits 1:
//
//   the emitted module is not valid wasm … type mismatch:
//   expected i32, found (ref $type)
//
// (No byte offset quoted on purpose: it moves with the seed.)
//
// THE MECHANISM. `structIndexOfObjCtx` resolves `{ r: 7 }` by field-name set with
// `anonValueFitsField`'s refutation-only widening (a union-BOX field accepts every atom), so
// the literal takes `Circle`'s row and its `r` is emitted BOXED. The CHECKER meanwhile types
// the binding `{r: i32}[]`, provable in one line — `if (lv1[0]).r != null { … }` is a LOUD
// "cannot compare i32 with null". The adoption also SUPPRESSES the row that would have
// agreed: `collectAnonShapes` interns an `#anon` row only `if structIndexOfObj(ai) < 0`.
//
// WHY THIS ONE AND NOT ANOTHER — and the selection rule is the one the genealogy in
// `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` earned. Its predecessor (D282) was chosen for stability
// against BOTH mechanisms of the variant⇄struct heap-merge family, and was closed by a third
// reading of the same argument. So this one is chosen from OUTSIDE that family entirely:
// **it declares no union**, so `uVariants` is empty, `armLayoutContested` is false,
// `variantStructHeapTwinAt` and `uVarSTwin` are never called at all (counted at the site:
// `entries=0`), and `emitUnionCoerce` is unreachable. Every mechanism that has closed a
// specimen in this genealogy since D33 is structurally inapplicable, not merely untried.
//
// IT IS ALSO THE MOST-ATTACKED OPEN ROW IN THE INVENTORY, which is the second half of the
// rule. `silent-class-inventory.md` D209 carries TWO candidate fixes BUILT, MEASURED AND
// REFUSED — the RESOLVER side and the READ side — each refuted by a program it takes from
// `runs` to check-clean invalid wasm, and each pinned as its own refutation row (D271 and
// D272, fixtures in `anon-literal-adopted-by-a-declared-box-field.vl`). "Stable against
// every candidate so far" is evidence about the candidates and not about the specimen; two
// candidates that were built, priced and declined is evidence about the specimen.
//
// THE NAMED SUCCESSOR, so the next swap is a two-line edit and not a re-derivation:
// `silent-class-inventory.md` **D224** — D211's arm-twin quarter, whose own fix is likewise
// BUILT and refused at a measured 207 census cells (`scripts/silent-sweep/census/d224-cost.json`).
//
// PRE-EXISTING, MEASURED RATHER THAN INHERITED: graded `check-clean invalid wasm` on this
// change's merge base (seed 1,463,065) and on its shipped seed (1,463,113), same sentence,
// and its module is BYTE-IDENTICAL across the change.
//
// IT IS THE SPECIMEN. This file is kept byte-for-byte identical to
// `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts`'s `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` below its header, which needs a
// program that type-checks clean and whose module the engine refuses.
//
// WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates), which is the point:
// delete it, graduate a `@run` row, and swap `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` for another live member of
// the class. READ THE NOTE IN `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` BEFORE DOING THAT — including
// what it says about where to look before concluding the class is empty.
type Circle = { r: i32 | null }
const lv1 = [{ r: 7 }]
print((lv1[0]).r)
